 its seals on main's .gitignore (the framework's thin path, T12; P-885; main's
 M76, M77): an opened ledger stays along the history; round n is opened before
 round n + 1 is sealed; a seat's content sighted after the opening is reported
 as opened early and not counted; an expectation is a seat's content, for
 sealed late and opened early; the ledger's round said to be a batch of cards;
 a test that main's .gitignore ignores neither the seals nor a ledger; tests
 fail with each hole put back

